#!/bin/sh
#
# system-splash is intentionally DISABLED on rk3326.
#
# The boot visual on rk3326 is provided by progressbar_rk (launched from
# /etc/init.d/rcS), which renders the boot logo AND the progress bar directly to
# /dev/fb0. The stock batocera/knulli system-splash uses fbv to blit a PNG to
# the same /dev/fb0, so running it here would fight progressbar_rk for the
# framebuffer (fbv would overwrite the progress bar). This no-op overrides the
# knulli-splash package's S03system-splash for all rk3326 boards.
#
exit 0
